From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rama Bondan Prakoso <ramanarubp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Set twrp.storage.ready after fstab processing (OrangeFox)

OrangeFox does not set twrp.storage.ready, so init never starts mobicore,
tee-service, gatekeeper and KeyMint on X6871. keystore2 then never registers
and the recovery blocks forever during decryption at the logo.

Decryption runs inside Setup_Fstab_Partitions(), so set the property right
after Process_Fstab() succeeds instead of after Setup_Fstab_Partitions().
---
diff --git a/twrp.cpp b/twrp.cpp
index 498ea9e..c0a5717 100644
--- a/twrp.cpp
+++ b/twrp.cpp
@@ -541,6 +541,11 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+	// Fstab processing and its temporary mount cleanup are done. Setting this
+	// before Setup_Fstab_Partitions(), which blocks in decryption, lets init
+	// start the Trustonic stack (see init.tee.rc and init.recovery.mt6895.rc).
+	property_set("twrp.storage.ready", "1");
+
 	// Set the props for OrangeFox dynamic partitions
 	//PartitionManager.Fox_Set_Dynamic_Partition_Props();
 
